  "title": "Capturing live events for Apple Immersive Video: Learnings from \"Metallica\"",
  "description": "Learn how to approach large-scale live events for Apple Immersive Video. This session covers the importance of access, mapping stage layouts, placing cameras effectively, and analyzing previous performances to anticipate the show. Using the Apple Immersive title \"Metallica\" as an example, you’ll also see how pre-vis in Apple Vision Pro and stabilized capture systems help capture dynamic performances while maintaining comfort.\n\nThis session was originally presented as part of the Meet with Apple activity “Create immersive media experiences for visionOS - Day 2.” Watch the full video for more insights and related sessions.",
